rows=[
f(73,'Skew-information inequality fails for the stated arbitrary CPTP channel','Source defines I_rho(H)=Tr(rho H²)-Tr(sqrt(rho)Hsqrt(rho)H) and claims I_E(rho)(E(H))<=I_rho(H). Take rho=diag(1/3,2/3), H=P0, E(A)=A00 P0+A11 Pplus. Kraus K0=|0><0| and K1=|+><1| sum KdaggerK=I. E(H)=H, but E(rho)=[[2/3,1/3],[1/3,1/3]], so I grows from0 to1/15. Both states are positive definite. This is not the correctly transported tangent-vector monotonicity theorem.',[e(351,172,177)],'Remove or restrict this inequality with exact channel/observable hypotheses and proof; separate skew information from general monotone metric contraction. Retain this negative control.','CHECK-050 verifies complete channel/state/observable, positive square root identity and rational terms2/3-3/5=1/15.','high'),
f(74,'Closed overlap differences are incorrectly called pairwise agreement','Reference first defines omega=delta0(local observations), then calls delta1 omega=0 pairwise consistency. For local values0,1,2 on a triangle, edge differences1,1,-2 are nonzero but sum0. Such omega is already exact by definition; its closed-survivor branch cannot occur without changing the supplied data model. Nilpotence, closedness, exactness and agreement are distinct predicates.',[e(354,20,24),e(351,63,67)],'Define independent edge data when closed nonexact classes are intended; test delta0(local)=0 for agreement. Require image/kernel equality for exactness, not only d²=0. The skill phrase exact complexes with d²=0 may impose both, so do not treat its wording alone as a proved false implication.','CHECK-051/052 separate nilpotence from exactness and closedness from zero differences.','high'),
f(75,'Nonzero H1 group is not equivalent to missing global sections','Source asserts no global sections iff H1 is nonzero, including a Set-valued presheaf without an abelianization/support construction. Constant Q coefficients on a circle have H1=Q and many global constant sections. A particular contextuality obstruction class, empirical support and the whole cohomology group must not be identified.',[e(351,105,107),e(354,55,62)],'Specify empirical model, support/distribution extension problem, coefficient construction and distinguished obstruction class; state only the direction and completeness theorem actually justified.','CHECK-053 supplies explicit incidence matrix, rank2, H1 dimension1 and global zero section.','high'),
f(76,'Discrete Wigner expression lacks normalization and characteristic restriction','With the displayed phase-point convention, Tr A=1 and maximally mixed rho=I/d gives the displayed W=1/d at d² points, summing to d. Standard normalized W needs an additional1/d. The exponent also uses inverse2 for every prime d, which is undefined in characteristic2.',[e(351,69,76)],'State odd-prime/odd-prime-power domain and consistent displacement/phase-point/Wigner conventions; test total mass and marginals before using contextuality conclusions.','CHECK-057 computes the d=3 maximally mixed normalization failure.'),
f(77,'General-poset and cross-domain obstruction formulas omit required structure','Galois connections yield an upper closure operator, but subtraction c-gamma(alpha(c)) is undefined for general posets. Truncation A->||A||n is a unit map, not generally an inclusion. Displayed lifting problem also asks a map X->E to extend f:A->B without specifying a lift on A or base extension on X.',[e(351,105,107),e(354,11,16),e(354,42,53)],'Keep the valid order closure statement; admit extra additive/metric structure before a numerical residual. Repair types and local-coefficient/simplicity hypotheses before claiming universal obstruction unification.'),
f(78,'SUSY note promotes determinant equality and superalgebra into missing guarantees','Equality det J=det DF does not force a positive determinant; superalgebra {Q,Qdagger}=2H alone does not force every state to be annihilated by Q. A zero-energy state premise would be needed. The note supplies no boundary-map bridge from this algebra to simplicial nilpotence and lists3D Pachner counts under a4D heading.',[e(353,16,30)],'Require explicit admitted complexes, determinant sign/domain conditions, zero-energy constraint and chain-map proof; use dimension-correct moves and treat sampled positivity as finite evidence.','CHECK-054/055/056 provide negative determinant, two-state supercharge and facet-count controls.','high'),
f(79,'Schema conformer upgrades evidence labels and drops valid quoted aliases','The mechanical MANUAL->VERIFIED migration map claims test/source verification without running or binding any verification. Alias regex recognizes double quoting only, so a valid single-quoted gt alias is dropped. Delimiter scanning can treat a later Markdown horizontal rule as frontmatter.',[e(352,13,26),e(352,80,84),e(352,111,147)],'Keep evidence status unchanged unless fresh owner evidence is supplied; parse actual anchored frontmatter losslessly, preserve aliases and original bytes, and generate reviewable changes before writes.','CHECK-058 isolates the actual alias regex; source inspection establishes unconditional status rewrite.','high'),
f(80,'Quantum/gauge unification confuses conditional, geometric and dynamical claims','Nonzero curvature need not give nonidentity holonomy on every chosen loop (an abelian flux2pi is a counterexample). One amplitude vector sqrt(probability) exp(i phase) does not encode every mixed density operator. P rho P is unnormalized postselection unless divided by its probability. Failure of a time-homogeneous semigroup does not alone prove non-Markovian memory; a time-dependent unitary propagator can be CP-divisible.',[e(354,72,89)],'Name the admitted bundle/local trivialization, loop, instrument and conditioning convention; distinguish pure-state encoding, mixed states, homogeneous semigroups and CP-divisibility. Supply actual cochain maps rather than assigning C1 by label.'),
f(81,'Quotient verifier lacks the laws named by its stages','Slot colours alone do not establish planar associativity; the quotient relation and congruence needed for well-defined composition are unspecified, and a Convention parameter appears outside the declared colour inventory. Three-run contraction wording repeats the shared-specification contradiction.',[e(342,1,90)],'Declare operations, identities/composition, quotient relation, congruence and associativity witnesses. Separate type checking, finite execution and universal invariants; defer to the stronger shared meta boundary.'),
f(82,'Lifecycle registers disagree on admitted versus pending skills','Current register labels four entries307--310 pending review although the same skill names occur admitted in archived entries302--305; the recommended queue says none through306. README inert-draft wording also differs from promotion claims. These are incompatible snapshots without an event-bound lifecycle record.',[e(328,1,16),e(330,1,10),e(339,1,75),e(340,270,315),e(341,1,23)],'Preserve historical registers and identify effective version/time with per-package evidence; use one append-only lifecycle ledger rather than silently treating every label as current.')]
